  "description": {
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Entandrophragma utile",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Entandrophragma_utile",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1323813371,
      "text": "Entandrophragma utile, called the sipo or utile, is a species of large tree in the genus Entandrophragma, native to nearly all of tropical Africa facing the Atlantic, from Guinea to Angola, and as far east as Uganda. The timber is traded as a tropical hardwood. It is sometimes called sipo mahogany. It shares many of the characteristics of genuine mahogany and is used as an alternative."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Entandrophragma utile",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Entandrophragma_utile",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 160878997,
      "text": "Entandrophragma utile, con nombre corriente sipo o aiele, es una especie de árbol perteneciente a la familia Meliaceae. Es originaria de África tropical."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Entandrophragma utile",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Entandrophragma_utile",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 234929023,
      "text": "Le Sipo est un très grand arbre de la famille des Meliaceae. On le trouve dans la forêt dense africaine, son bois est très utilisé en menuiserie extérieure, en ébénisterie, pour le contreplaqué."
    }
